From: =?UTF-8?q?Dirk=20J=C3=A4ckel?= <github@dirk.jaeckel.name>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 08:36:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] p2p: outbound-only node option: no listener, no UPnP, no
 external address

Myotis: the change of https://github.com/freedom-hq/ant/pull/276 (issue #269),
rebased onto b138f6bc074d8c28149017d4e7b1e80db8c67d4d and limited to the vendored
files (the PR's docs/ffi-parity-audit.md row is left out). Drop this patch when
upstream has merged the PR (rust/vendor/ant/VENDORED.md, "Patches").

An embedder that only fetches (a wallet reading a few chunks) should not
open an inbound port, map one on the user's router over UPnP, or announce
its public address to peers. `RunConfig::outbound_only` (and
`NodeConfig::outbound_only` / `with_outbound_only`) turns all three off:

- no `listen_on`;
- the UPnP behaviour is a disabled `Toggle`, so no SSDP search and no
  port mapping;
- no external address is registered from a listener or from a peer's
  `observed_addr`, and external addresses configured for such a node are
  refused at start (`RunError::Config`) rather than silently dropped;
- the "no globally-routable external address" warning is skipped.

The default (`false`) is unchanged. Peers still see the address of the
connection we dial them from, and the BZZ handshake echoes it back to them
as our underlay, signed with our BZZ key (`observed_underlay` in the Ack),
as for any node behind NAT.

Closes #269

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
